  "note": "Nebuchadnezzar's hall. The throne sits on its dais at the north end of the carpet runner; two rows of cedar columns flank it. The carpet is floor, not obstacle. The door in the south wall (x 850-1070) is the way in and out. Tall props are blocked at their base only, not over their whole drawn block: the part of a tent or a column that rises up the screen is what the player walks behind, and blocking all of it would make walk-behind unreachable. Flat-topped buildings seen from directly above (the city houses, the burnt sanctuary, the palace front) keep full-block collision, and their overlays are therefore inert by design.",
